nL112: Appearance settings\nL113: You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL114: \nL115:   1. cite61†Tencent-Hunyuan L116:   2. cite62†HY-WorldPlay L117: ## Repository navigation\nL118: \nL119:   *   * cite62†Code L120:   * cite63†Issues26 (26) L121:   * cite64†Pull requests3 (3) L122:   * cite65†Actions L123:   * cite66†Projects L124:   * cite67†Security and quality L125:   * cite68†Insights L126: \nL127: More items\nL128: \nL129: ## Files Expand file tree\nL130: \nL131: main\nL132: \nL133: ## Breadcrumbs\nL134: \nL135:   1. cite69†HY-WorldPlay L136:   2. /cite70†worldcompass L137: \nL138: /\nL139: \nL140: # README.md\nL141: \nL142: Copy path\nL143: \nL144: [Input: Go to file]\nL145: \nL146: Blame More file actions\nL147: \nL148: Blame More file actions\nL149: \nL150: ## Latest commit\nL151: \nL152: \nL153: \nL154: ## History\nL155: \nL156: History\nL157: \nL158: main\nL159: \nL160: ## Breadcrumbs\nL161: \nL162:   1. cite69†HY-WorldPlay L163:   2. /cite70†worldcompass L164: \nL165: /\nL166: # README.md\nL167: \nL168: Copy path\nL169: \nL170: Top\nL171: \nL172: ## File metadata and controls\nL173: \nL174:   * Preview\nL175: \nL176:   * Code\nL177: \nL178:   * Blame\nL179: \nL180: 339 lines (236 loc) · 10.2 KB\nL181: \nL182: cite71†Raw L183: \nL184: Copy raw file\nL185: \nL186: Download raw file\nL187: \nL188: Outline\nL189: \nL190: Edit and raw actions\nL191: \nL192: # 🧭 WorldCompass: Reinforcement Learning for Long-Horizon World Models\nL193: \nL194: cite72†English | cite73†简体中文 L195: \nL196: ## Introduction to WorldCompass\nL197: \nL198: WorldCompass uses Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) idea to improve action-following and visual quality in autoregressive video generation.\nL199: \nL200: cite74†Research Paper†arxiv.org L201: ## Training Guidence\nL202: \nL203: The training pipeline includes:\nL204: \nL205:   1. Environment Setup - Install dependencies\nL206:   2. Model Download - Download pretrained checkpoints\nL207:   3. Dataset Preparation - Prepare image-text latents and action trajectories\nL208:   4. Training - Run reinforcement learning training\nL209: \nL210: * * *\nL211: ### Step 1: Environment Setup\nL212: \nL213: * * *\nL214: \nL215: 1.1 Create Conda Environment\nL216: \nL217:     # Create and activate environment\nL218:     conda create -n worldcompass python=3.10 -y\nL219:     conda activate worldcompass\nL220: \nL221:     # Install dependencies\nL222:     pip install -r requirements.txt\nL223:     pip install transformers==4.50.0\nL224: \nL225:     # Install Flash Attention (recommended for faster training)\nL226:     pip install flash-attn==2.7.3 --no-build-isolation\nL227: \nL228: * * *\nL229: ### Step 2: Model Preparation\nL230: \nL231: * * *\nL232: \nL233: 2.1 Download Model Checkpoints\nL234: \nL235:     # Download all required models\nL236:     python download_models_worldcompass.py --hf_token <your_huggingface_token> --cache_dir <your_cache_dir>\nL237: \nL238: Note: You need access to FLUX.1-Redux-dev for the vision encoder:\nL239: \nL240:   1. Request access: cite75†https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-Redux-dev†huggingface.co L241:   2. Create token: cite76†https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens†huggingface.co (select \"Read\" permission)\nL242: The script will download:\nL243: \nL244:   * HunyuanVideo-1.5 base model (VAE, scheduler, 480p transformer)\nL245:   * HY-WorldPlay action models (AR model, bidirectional model, distilled model)\nL246:   * Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct text encoder\nL247:   * ByT5 encoders (byt5-small + Glyph-SDXL-v2)\nL248:   * SigLIP vision encoder (from FLUX.1-Redux-dev)\nL249:   * DepthAnythingV3 camera pose estimation model - Option 1\nL250:   * Hunyuan-WorldMirror camera pose estimation model - Option 2\nL251: \nL252: * * *\nL253: 2.2 Clone DepthAnythingV3 Repository (Optional, Using WorldMirror as Reward by default)\nL254: \nL255:     git clone https://github.com/ByteDance-Seed/Depth-Anything-3.git DepthAnythingV3\nL256:     mv ./DepthAnythingV3/src/depth_anything_3 ./depth_anything_3\nL257: \nL258: * * *\nL259: ### Step 3: Dataset Preparation\nL260: \nL261: * * *\nL262: \nL263: 3.1 Prepare Input Data\nL264: \nL265: Create a JSON file containing your training data:\nL266: \nL267:     [\nL268:       {\nL269:         \"image_path\": \"/path/to/image1.jpg\",\nL270:         \"caption\": \"A serene park with trees and a bridge over water\"\nL271:       },\nL272:       {\nL273:         \"image_path\": \"/path/to/image2.png\",\nL274:         \"caption\": \"A modern city street at sunset\"\nL275:       }\nL276:     ]\nL277: \nL278: * * *\nL279: \nL280: 3.2 Extract Image-Text Latents\nL281: \nL282: This step encodes images and text into latent features using VAE and text encoders.\nL283: Single GPU:\nL284: \nL285:     python prepare_dataset/prepare_image_text_latent_simple.py \\\nL286:         --input_json /path/to/train.json \\\nL287:         --output_dir /path/to/train_latents \\\nL288:         --hunyuan_checkpoint_path /path/to/hunyuanvideo_1_5\nL289: \nL290: Multi-GPU (Recommended):\nL291: \nL292:     torchrun --nproc_per_node=8 prepare_dataset/prepare_image_text_latent_simple.py \\\nL293:         --input_json /path/to/train.json \\\nL294:         --output_dir /path/to/train_latents \\\nL295:         --hunyuan_checkpoint_path /path/to/hunyuanvideo_1_5\nL296: Output Structure:\nL297: \nL298:     `/path/to/train_latents/\nL299:     ├── latents/\nL300:     │   ├── 0_000000.pt\nL301:     │   ├── 0_000001.pt\nL302:     │   └── ...\nL303:     └── latents.json          # Index file for training\nL304:     `\nL305: \nL306: Each `.pt` file contains:\nL307:   * `latent`: VAE-encoded image features [1, C, T, H, W]\nL308:   * `image_cond`: First frame condition [1, C, 1, H, W]\nL309:   * `prompt_embeds`: Text embeddings [1, L, D]\nL310:   * `prompt_mask`: Text attention mask [1, L]\nL311:   * `vision_states`: Visual features [1, N, D]\nL312:   * `byt5_text_states`: ByT5 text features [1, 256, 1472]\nL313:   * `byt5_text_mask`: ByT5 attention mask [1, 256]\nL314: \nL315: * * *\nL316: \nL317: 3.3 Prepare Evaluation Data\nL318: To support observing model performance on a fixed subset during training, we recommend building a mini evaluation dataset. The JSON file format is the same as the training data. The recommended number should be divisible by the expected number of GPUs, and for efficiency, typically 16 or 32 samples are sufficient.\nL319: \nL320:     python prepare_dataset/prepare_image_text_latent_simple.py \\\nL321:         --input_json /path/to/eval.json \\\nL322:         --output_dir /path/to/eval_latents \\\nL323:         --hunyuan_checkpoint_path /path/to/hunyuanvideo_1_5\nL324: * * *\nL325: \nL326: 3.4 Generate Action Trajectories\nL327: \nL328: Generate random camera trajectory sequences for training:\nL329: \nL330:     python prepare_dataset/prepare_custom_action.py\nL331: \nL332: Default Output: `prepare_dataset/harder_random_poses.json` (1000 trajectories, 128 actions each, default settings favor generating complex composite actions)\nL333: \nL334: Customize: Edit `prepare_custom_action.py` to adjust number of trajectories and actions per trajectory, as well as trajectory template synthesis rules.\nL335: \nL336: * * *\nL337: ### Step 4: Start Training\nL338: \nL339: * * *\nL340: \nL341: 4.1 Configure Training Script\nL342: Modify the TODO configs in `scripts/train_worldcompass.sh`:\nL343: \nL344:     export MASTER_ADDR=\"\"       # [TODO] Set master address\nL345: \nL346:     # NOTE: Run download_models.py (Step 2) can get the exact paths for the variables below.\nL347:     CACHE_DIR=\"\"              # [TODO] Fill in the overall checkpoint cache directory (as printed by download_models.py)\nL348:     HUNYUAN_CHECKPOINT=\"\"     # [TODO] Fill in the HunYuan checkpoint directory\nL349:     WORLDPLAY_CHECKPOINT=\"\"   # [TODO] Fill in the WorldPlay checkpoint directory\nL350:     TRAIN_LATENTS_DIR=\"\"      # [TODO] Path to the train latents directory\nL351:     EVAL_LATENTS_DIR=\"\"       # [TODO] Path to the eval latents directory\nL352:     POSE_PATH=\"\"              # [TODO] Path to the custom action pose json\nL353:     OUTPUT_DIR=\"\"             # [TODO] Path to the output directory\nL354: \nL355:     --wandb_key \"\"            # [TODO] Set wandb key\nL356:     --wandb_entity \"\"         # [TODO] Set wandb entity\nL357: * * *\nL358: \nL359: 4.2 Training!!!\nL360: \nL361: Training on 8 GPUs can show initial improvements, but more nodes typically result in more stable training and better final results.\nL362: \nL363: Single Node (8 GPUs):\nL364: \nL365:     bash scripts/train_worldcompass.sh 0 1\nL366: Multi-Node Training:\nL367: \nL368:     # On each node, run with appropriate rank\nL369:     # Node 0 (master):\nL370:     bash scripts/train_worldcompass.sh 0 4  # 4 nodes total\nL371: \nL372:     # Node 1:\nL373:     bash scripts/train_worldcompass.sh 1 4\nL374: \nL375:     # Node 2:\nL376:     bash scripts/train_worldcompass.sh 2 4\nL377: \nL378:     # Node 3:\nL379:     bash scripts/train_worldcompass.sh 3 4\nL380: \nL381: Note: Ensure all nodes can communicate via `MASTER_ADDR` and `MASTER_PORT`.\nL382: \nL383: 4.3 Monitor Training\nL384: Training logs and checkpoints will be saved to:\nL385: \nL386:     `${CKPT_DIR}/${exp_name}/\nL387:     ├── checkpoint-{step}/\nL388:     │   ├── transformer/\nL389:     │   │   └── diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors\nL390:     │   └── training_state.pt\nL391:     └── generated_videos/           # Sample videos during training\nL392:     `\nL393: \nL394: If WandB is configured, metrics will be logged to your WandB dashboard.\nL395: ### 4.4 Hardware Requirements\nL396: \nL397: Our experiments were conducted on GPUs with 96GB memory. If you encounter GPU OOM issues, consider:\nL398: \nL399:   * Reducing `window_frames`\nL400:   * Converting VAE to `torch.bf16` (may cause training instability)\nL401: ## Results\nL402: \nL403: We have conducted comprehensive validation on the WorldPlay baseline model. Our evaluation demonstrates that after undergoing WorldCompass post-training, the model's capabilities undergo a qualitative leap, particularly in both interaction following and visual quality.\nL404: ## 📚 Citation\nL405: \nL406:     @article{hyworld2025,\nL407:       title={HY-World 1.5: A Systematic Framework for Interactive World Modeling with Real-Time Latency and Geometric Consistency},\nL408:       author={Team HunyuanWorld},\nL409:       journal={arXiv preprint},\nL410:       year={2025}\nL411:     }\nL412: \nL413:     @article{wang2026worldcompass,\nL414:       title={WorldCompass: Reinforcement Learning for Long-Horizon World Models},\nL415:       author={Wang, Zehan and Wang, Tengfei and Zhang, Haiyu and Zuo, Xuhui and Wu, Junta and Wang, Haoyuan and Sun, Wenqiang and Wang, Zhenwei and Cao, Chenjie and Zhao, Hengshuang and others},\nL416:       journal={arXiv preprint},\nL417:       year={2026}\nL418:     }\nL419: \nL420:     @article{worldplay2025,\nL421:         title={WorldPlay: Towards Long-Term Geometric Consistency for Real-Time Interactive World Model},\nL422:         author={Wenqiang Sun and Haiyu Zhang and Haoyuan Wang and Junta Wu and Zehan Wang and Zhenwei Wang and Yunhong Wang and Jun Zhang and Tengfei Wang and Chunchao Guo},\nL423:         year={2025},\nL424:         journal={arXiv preprint}\nL425:     }\nL426: ## Contact\nL427: \nL428: Please send emails to tengfeiwang12@gmail.com if there is any question\nL429: \nL430: ## 🙏 Acknowledgements\nL431: \nL432: We would like to thank cite77†HunyuanWorld , cite78†HunyuanWorld-Mirror , cite79†HunyuanVideo , cite80†DiffusionNFT and cite81†FastVideo for their great work.\nL433: \nL434: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2602.09022] WorldCompass: Reinforcement Learning for Long-Horizon World Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.09022)\nciteturn32169view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn32168view2\",\"lineno\":8}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 9 Feb 2026]\nL9: # Title:WorldCompass: Reinforcement Learning for Long-Horizon World Models\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Zehan Wang , cite6†Tengfei Wang , cite7†Haiyu Zhang , cite8†Xuhui Zuo , cite9†Junta Wu , cite10†Haoyuan Wang , cite11†Wenqiang Sun , cite5†Zhenwei Wang , cite12†Chenjie Cao , cite13†Hengshuang Zhao , cite14†Chunchao Guo , cite15†Zhou Zhao L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled WorldCompass: Reinforcement Learning for Long-Horizon World Models, by Zehan Wang and 11 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite16†View PDF cite17†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:This work presents WorldCompass, a novel Reinforcement Learning (RL) post-training framework for the long-horizon, interactive video-based world models, enabling them to explore the world more accurately and consistently based on interaction signals.\nL17: To effectively \"steer\" the world model's exploration, we introduce three core innovations tailored to the autoregressive video generation paradigm: 1) Clip-level rollout Strategy: We generate and evaluate multiple samples at a single target clip, which significantly boosts rollout efficiency and provides fine-grained reward signals.\nL18: 2) Complementary Reward Functions: We design reward functions for both interaction-following accuracy and visual quality, which provide direct supervision and effectively suppress reward-hacking behaviors. 3) Efficient RL Algorithm: We employ the negative-aware fine-tuning strategy coupled with various efficiency optimizations to efficiently and effectively enhance model capacity.\nL19: Evaluations on the SoTA open-source world model, WorldPlay, demonstrate that WorldCompass significantly improves interaction accuracy and visual fidelity across various scenarios.\nL20: Comments:  | Project page: \\url{cite18†this https URL†3d-models.hunyuan.tencent.com }\nL21: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite19†arXiv:2602.09022 [cs.CV]\nL23:    | (or cite20†arXiv:2602.09022v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL24:    | cite21†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.09022†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Zehan Wang [cite22†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Mon, 9 Feb 2026 18:59:47 UTC (8,579 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled WorldCompass: Reinforcement Learning for Long-Horizon World Models, by Zehan Wang and 11 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite16†View PDF L37:   * cite17†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite23†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite24†view license L41: \nL42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: cs.CV\nL45: \nL46: cite25†< prev |   cite26†next > L47: \nL48: cite27†new | cite28†recent | cite29†2026-02 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite30†cs L53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite31†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite32†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite33†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmark\nL70: \nL71: [I